{{!-- The inventory as the printed Cairn sheet draws it: `slotsMax` numbered ruled lines, always
      all of them. An empty slot is a line, not nothing — which is why this layout has no dead
      space to leave. A *bulky* item (or a stack) occupies as many numbered lines as it has slots;
      the printed sheet draws that as one block two lines tall rather than a row plus a
      continuation mark, and so does this. *Petty* occupies none and has its own tab.

      Never an eleventh line. Ten is a hard cap enforced on the documents (`module/documents/
      item.js`, `actor.js`): a write that would not fit is refused before it lands, so there is
      no "over capacity" for a sheet to draw.

      The column of circles down the right is the printed sheet's Fatigue track: one circle per
      slot. The ledger, the circles and the word FATIGUE stand inside ONE drawn frame, with an
      upright between the ledger and the track — the word belongs to the structure, not beside it. An occupied circle is inert — Fatigue cannot be marked over a thing being carried —
      so with all ten slots full there is nothing to click, which is the rule:
      "If a character is forced to add Fatigue to their inventory but they have no free slots,
      they must drop an item" (`srd-2e/players-guide/core-rules.md`). --}}
<div class="cairn-slot-block" data-ink="box" data-ink-seed="ledger" data-ink-w="1.4" data-ink-a="0.5">
    {{!-- The body lines: what the character attacks with that is not carried. Inside the same
          frame, because they are read with the ten, but with no number, because they are not
          slots — and no Fatigue circle, because a Fatigue is never marked over a claw. Unarmed
          is always the first: every character has fists and no item stands for them. A natural
          thing's line is the slot line's own anatomy, name opening the item and the shared
          control cluster at its end; it is always to hand, so its name is always bold. --}}
    <ol class="cairn-slot-list cairn-body-list">
        <li class="cairn-slot cairn-body-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="body-unarmed" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-at="bottom">
            <span class="cairn-slot-number"></span>
            <span class="cairn-slot-body">
                <span class="cairn-item-name-and-tags">
                    <span class="cairn-item-title"><strong>{{localize 'CAIRN.Unarmed'}}</strong></span>
                    <span class="cairn-item-tag">d4 {{localize 'CAIRN.Damage'}}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="cairn-item-controls">
                    <a data-action="rollUnarmed" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.RollDamageHint'}}"><i class="fas fa-dice-d20"></i></a>
                </span>
            </span>
        </li>
        {{#each inventory.body as |item|}}
        <li class="cairn-slot cairn-body-row draggable" data-item-id="{{item.id}}"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="body-{{item.id}}" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-at="bottom">
            <span class="cairn-slot-number"></span>
            <span class="cairn-slot-body">
                <span class="cairn-item-name-and-tags" data-action="itemEdit">
                    <span class="cairn-item-title"><strong>{{item.name}}</strong></span>
                    {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/item-tags.hbs" system=item.system inBody=true}}
                    {{#if item.showUses}}{{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/item-uses.hbs" uses=item.usesDisplay editable=@root.editable}}{{/if}}
                </span>
                {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/item-controls.hbs" item=item editable=@root.editable}}
            </span>
        </li>
        {{/each}}
    </ol>
    {{!-- The second stroke of a double rule, under the last body line's own: the printed sheet's
          way of closing one section before the next begins, so slot 1 visibly starts here. --}}
    <div class="cairn-body-rule" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="body-rule" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42"></div>

    {{!-- The ten, with the Fatigue track beside them. The upright and the word are placed against
          this box rather than the whole frame, so neither runs up past slot 1 into the body
          lines. --}}
    <div class="cairn-ledger">
        {{!-- The upright that separates the ledger from the Fatigue track. It is absolutely placed
              rather than a column of its own, because the circles live inside the rows — see
              `.cairn-fatigue-rule` in the stylesheet for the arithmetic. --}}
        <span class="cairn-fatigue-rule" data-ink="vline" data-ink-seed="fatigue-rule" data-ink-w="1" data-ink-a="0.3"></span>
        <ol class="cairn-slot-list">
            {{#each inventory.rows as |row|}}
            {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/slot-row.hbs" row=row}}
            {{/each}}
        </ol>
        <span class="cairn-fatigue-label">{{localize 'CAIRN.Fatigue'}}</span>
    </div>
</div>

